-- 1134: PCB assembly calculators -- the SMT line (print, SPI, placement, reflow, AOI), through-hole insertion and soldering, test and depanel.
--
-- GENERATED by scripts/generate-pcb-calculators-migration.ts from
-- src/modules/bom-items/costing/pcb/calculators/pcb-calculators.json.
-- Do not edit by hand: change the spec and regenerate.
--
-- ROOT CAUSE
--
-- A board with components was priced as a bare board: the PCB catalog had no assembly process and no calculator for one. Migration 1133
-- seeded the SMT line, through-hole and test machines (USA, India) and the sourced assembly reference (memory/PCBA/Assembly), and the
-- catalog's assembly processes. These are their calculators: each times one board from the board files' counts (placements, joints,
-- nets, the array) and the sourced rates; the line changeover, the line's wait on its slowest machine, the solder paste and the ICT
-- fixture are helpers the engine runs per board, which no operation maps to.
--
-- This migration creates one global calculator per spec entry (inputs are the
-- values the cost engine seeds, each shown with its source in the calculation
-- trace; calculated fields are the formulas the engine evaluates, it holds
-- none) and links every PCB catalog operation it computes to its
-- calculator in process_calculator_mappings.
--
-- Requires migration 804 (calculators.retired_at).
-- Self-contained, idempotent, post-checked.

BEGIN;

